  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1100 AM MDT Fri Jun 19 2026\n\nLooks like we are entering a more static weather pattern in the \nmid/long term as the mid and upper highs become stacked over \nnorthern Mexico and the Baja. In the short term for today we \ncontinue with the mid level high over southern New Mexico. Most of\nthe deeper layered moisture that was over the CWA Thursday has \nvanished in place this morning. Dewpoints are already lowering, \nwith 30s west mixing out as far east as the RG Valley this \nafternoon. Best moisture will remain over Otero/Hudspeth Counties,\nwith afternoon dewpoints still in the 40s to 50 and PWs around \none inch. Thus isolated afternoon thunderstorms look plausible for\nthe Sacs and Hudspeth Co, with a few over Hudspeth lasting into \nearly evening.\n\nAforementioned static pattern will turn up the heat knob after \ntoday. While today will see near 100 El Paso metro area and lower \nvalley, high temps Saturday through much of next will gradually \nwarm, with Tue-Fri looking to be the hottest. NBM MOS temps for \nthis period run from 103-107 across the lowlands. 90th percentile \nhighs for the same period range from 105-110. Needless to say we \nare probably looking at several days of Heat Advisories and could \napproach Excessive Heat Warnings as we enter the two week window \nof hottest temperatures climatologically.",
